{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. I've called us together because we have a decision to make before Thursday's medical-device housing run. As you know, our available virgin polymer won't be enough to complete the planned batch, but there is a lot of reclaimed pellets in the materials cage that hasn't been authorized for this product yet. Before I make any final authorization decision, I need quality and environmental-compliance sign-off per plant policy. I'd like to hear from each of you on where we stand on that, and on whether the reclaimed material can meet the controls we need for a regulated-product run."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, Mara. I've completed my lab review on the reclaimed polymer lot. I can tell you right now that the reclaimed material is suitable for this housing, but only under specific conditions — there's a required blend ratio and a mandatory first-article testing requirement that I need to formally share with the group. I also need to flag that the lab result documentation hasn't been attached to the production traveler yet, which is a gap we'll need to close before the run begins. Let me go ahead and put those specifics on the record now."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I need to put something critical on the record before we go any further. Late yesterday I received a revised safety data sheet from the supplier that has not yet been entered in the plant's chemical register. My review of that revised SDS classifies the reclaimed lot's additive residue as regulated process waste. That means any use of this material triggers labeled segregated storage requirements and a hazardous-waste manifest for any discarded pellets or purge material. This directly affects the environmental-compliance sign-off Mara needs from me, and it also has implications for the waste and storage controls the plant normally records before a regulated-product run begins."}
```

